:: The Anchor [event main_quest] {"position":"4950,500","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "The Anchor" (main_anchor), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 4.8. After a week of $sister.callName's attention (Be Nice to $brian.name),
   $brian.name is easy to talk to. I ask him for a small handheld: one emitter, a short burst at full strength, a profile I
   write myself. He's flustered and eager and doesn't ask a single question about what it's for. His only worry is the coil:
   two bursts, maybe, before it cooks (the device's two uses, maxUses in Define Company). $ethan.name sees the parts order on
   the shared sheet and says nothing. The quest's set unlocks project_company_anchor (only $brian.name works on it) and ends
   her Extra Friendly task. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[14].img>><</silent>>
$brian.name has changed this week. It's small. He says good morning to people now, to their faces, or at least to their shoulders. He's started wearing shirts that have buttons. Yesterday $ethan.name told a joke about a capacitor and $brian.name laughed out loud and then looked around, startled, as if somebody else had done it.

A week of $sister.callName pulling up a chair to his desk did that. I asked her to be nice to him, and she was, and now he's the most approachable he's going to get.

So I pull up the same chair.

<<linkreplace "Talk to $brian.name">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $brian, text: "Oh. Hi. Hey. Uh, is something broken?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Nothing's broken. I want you to build me something." },
{ text: "He sits up a little. Behind his glasses his eyes do the thing they do when a problem walks into the room: they get bright." },
{ who: $player, text: "Small. Handheld. Something that fits in a jacket pocket. One emitter, not an array. Focused, short range. And it doesn't need to run for hours. It needs to run for a minute, at full output, and then it can rest." },
{ who: $brian, text: "Full output." },
{ who: $player, text: "Everything the emitter can give, in one burst. I'll write the profile myself." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I wait for the question. Any engineer would ask it. What's it for? Why full output? What happens to whoever's standing in front of it?

$brian.name pushes his glasses up his nose and pulls a notepad toward him and starts drawing.

<<linkreplace "Let him draw">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $brian, text: "Okay. Okay. So one emitter at full output, that's, uh, that's a lot of current through a very small coil. It'll get hot. Really hot." },
{ who: $brian, text: "You'd need a capacitor bank to dump it all at once. That's most of the charge, gone. One burst, full drain. Maybe two, if the coil holds up, but I wouldn't, uh, I wouldn't count on more than two before it cooks." },
{ who: $player, text: "Two is enough." },
{ who: $brian, text: "Two is enough. Okay. Then I'd put the bank here, and the coil here, and a ceramic shield on this side so it doesn't, uh. So it points the right way." },
{ text: "He draws an arrow on the sketch, pointing away from the handle. He doesn't draw anything at the other end of the arrow. He doesn't ask what goes there." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

He talks for ten minutes about coils. I understand about half of it, and I don't need to understand the rest. What I need is the thing he isn't doing, which is asking. He's happy. He's been given a hard, interesting problem by the boss whose $sister.relation has been bringing him coffee all week, and the last thing he wants to do is make it complicated.

<<linkreplace "Give him the project">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "It's yours. Just you. Not the team. Not $ethan.name. I want one person who knows exactly how it's built." },
{ who: $brian, text: "Just me." },
{ text: "He goes very slightly red. I think it's the nicest thing anyone has said to him in this building." },
{ who: $brian, text: "Okay. I'll, uh. I'll order the parts today. It's mostly stuff we have. The coil's custom. Two weeks, maybe less." },
{ who: $player, text: "What do we call it?" },
{ who: $brian, text: "I don't know. It's, uh. It holds one thing in place. Really hard. Like an anchor." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

Like an anchor. He has no idea how right he is.

He tears the sketch off the pad, folds it in quarters and puts it in his shirt pocket, behind his pens, and goes back to his screen to start the parts list.

<<linkreplace "That afternoon">>
At four, the parts order shows up on the shared purchasing sheet everybody can see: a capacitor bank rated for something that should live in a car, a ceramic shield, a custom coil, and a housing the size of a deck of cards. Under "Project", $brian.name has typed <i>misc (important)</i>.

Across the office, $ethan.name has the sheet open. I can see it reflected in the window behind him. He scrolls down to the new lines and stops, and reads them, and his hand stays still on the mouse for a while.

Then he scrolls back up, closes the tab, and puts his headphones on. He doesn't say a word about it, to $brian.name or to me.

I go back to my email. It's a reasonable order for a hardware company. Anybody could have a reason.

<<run State.variables.brian.stats.morale = Math.clamp(State.variables.brian.stats.morale + 10, State.variables.brian.stats.min.morale, State.variables.brian.stats.max.morale)>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 2>>
<<NextQuest $player>>
<<run Notification.show("New project available: The Anchor (only " + $brian.name + " can work on it)", { type: Notification.INFORMATION })>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
